  "observations": {
    "negative": [
      "Every reproduced state.json differs from the sealed one, because Hermes records a run id, a creation time and the run directory; only maps, counts, exits, gates and reasons are compared.",
      "Hermes leaves an untracked .gas-snapshot in each anchor copy, so the anchor copies were not restored; they were deleted.",
      "In each rejection, Hermes also wrote after maps for contracts the sealed record does not commit (the selector run's HooksFactory layout, the layout run's WildcatArchController maps); only the committed after map is compared.",
      "The public copies and run directories were deleted after the run, so the digests reproduced for the three public anchors and both rejections are recorded only."
    ],
    "positive": [
      "Each of the five anchors re-ran its recorded baseline invocation on a fresh clone under env -i, exited 0 at baseline_ready with its sealed pass count, and every canonical layout, raw layout and method map it wrote has the sealed digest.",
      "Both selected Gate 5 candidates re-ran on fresh clones, passed Gates 1 to 4 and exited 50 at Gate 5 with the sealed reason; each copy's Gate 1 maps equal its anchor's sealed maps, the committed after map reproduced byte for byte, and the copy was clean at its pinned commit after restoration.",
      "Each rejection's gas-comparison.json reproduced with the committed digest."
    ]
  },
